[[File:Banshee icon.png|left]]
'''Twisted Banshees''' are stronger variants of [[banshee]]s that require level 15 [[Slayer]] to kill. They are found exclusively within the [[Catacombs of Kourend]], in a [[multicombat area]]. There is a safespot in the walkway between the two rooms. Players '''must''' wear [[earmuffs]] or a [[Slayer helmet]] while fighting them in order to avoid the effects of their screams, which cause the player to take 7 damage and have their stats greatly reduced in [[Attack]], [[Strength]], [[Defence]], [[Ranged]], [[Magic]], [[Prayer]], and [[Agility]] with every attack received. They use [[magical melee]], and their attacks are fairly accurate. These opponents seem to regenerate 1 hp each time they are attacked, regardless of whether or not your hit deals damage. As a result, [[Thralls|Thralls,]] especially the lesser variants, are not very effective when fighting Twisted banshees.

As they are undead, the [[Crumble Undead]] spell and the [[Salve amulet]] '''do''' work on them.

They are popular with Ironmen players due to good experience rates for their level along with dropping generous amounts of herbs, pure essence and various rune equipment.

A dwarf multi-cannon cannot be used to kill twisted banshees.

While on a banshee Slayer task, there is a 1/200 chance that a [[Screaming twisted banshee|Screaming Twisted Banshee]] will spawn after you kill a Twisted Banshee (if you have the [[Slayer Rewards|Bigger and Badder]] slayer reward unlocked). After claiming the elite tier rewards from the [[Combat Achievements]] system, this chance is increased to 1/150.

